# T013 warning: ambiguous type variable with source name display.
# When a function parameter has a constraint but the parameter's type variable
# doesn't appear in the return type, T013 should report both the user-visible
# parameter name and the internal TypeVar name for better diagnostics.
#
# This test verifies that when parameter 'x' has inferred TypeVar '_tN' with
# constraint [x: Comparable], the warning message includes both 'x' (user-visible)
# and the internal name for debugging.
[fn@[constraint: [x: Comparable] return: Int] [let x] 42]
=== out
Function(x)

=== warn
inferred type is Unknown — consider adding a type annotation
